beral  conservative but i i think it's possible  that someone like that could appear but  no the desantis mold is is the way the  party's going for sure or or maybe even  worse honestly maybe even tucker or  something to that effect well  in looking at some of these recent trump  rallies and cpac  what gets the most applause  is the overtly homophobic and  transphobic stuff like in watching cpac  the crowd was kind of dead  until  ted cruz ridiculed pronouns and i don't  remember who it was talked about trans  women in sports like the the applause  lines were the homophobic transphobic  applause lines trump now tells the story  about the weightlifting  and the swimmer you know it's the it's  these every single rally it's the same  stories is that surprising to see that  kind of resurface  i wouldn't say so it's disappointing  because  look we all play these games like in my  head  i felt like the gay rights  march was going forward and we those of  us on the pro gay rights side were  winning and so  you know i that it wasn't you know by  the time i really came into politics  like the writing was on the wall right  like the march for to progress was  marching forward and thank thank you to  all the people that did that fight  before we got there but but  i should have see we should have known  that there would be backsliding right  the types these people their hatreds  their cruelty they didn't go away you  know a lot of times the republicans get  caricatured as like being so stupid that  they don't know what they're doing  they're they're strategic they're  tactical if you'd listen to focus groups  or republican voters that they didn't  change their mind on gay marriage  they're just like well this is a loser  for us right like it's not worth  fighting it right now right it's a  political loser we're going to go win on  other issues that's why they moved on to  the trans stuff right  uh now with the with what desantis is  doing in the schools don't say gay the  pron